  "suspect_term_adjudication": "In the independent derivation, no analogue of the printed e_1 pair survives: the reduced kinetic coefficient contains no (J'^2 - J'^3)/X term (fit coefficient of the pair in Delta is -1.000 for each of T3, T4 separately -- parities differ, so they are determined independently). The odd member (T4) is the term F4-2 flagged; the even member (T3) is equally spurious. At u=0 the pair is the only source of left-right asymmetry AND of the negative-side ghost; with the pair removed the corrected K_0 is positive at both infinities (K_0/J^2 -> +2/tau^2 in App-B normalisation).",
  "verdict": "(B) GHOST IS AN ARTEFACT -- independent derivation from the covariant action gives K0^(ind) > 0 at every sampled radius in [-60,60] (min ~ 0 only at the throat, where K0 vanishes quadratically like F4-2's), G0^(ind) > 0 everywhere, and K0^(ind)/J^2 -> +1/tau^2 at BOTH infinities. The F4-2 ghost is produced by the printed Appendix B e_1 pair identified in delta_fit. The l=0 sector PASSES on the corrected coefficients. (M0^(ind) agrees with F4-2's M0/2 at sample radii, so F4-3's l=0 tachyon input is unaffected in the mass sector; its kinetic normalisation flips sign on the negative side, which F4-3 must use.)"
